  "description": "Ryan Nyquist is the longest standing member of the Haro Freestyle team and the Quist is a collaboration between Ryan, Haro and our product designers to create a totally custom complete. With Ryan's specific geometry to suit his park riding preferences, the Quist is a fine-tuned freestyle machine. Standard equipment includes a Gyro detangler for unlimited barspins. Ryan's personal touches are everywhere, from the Vivid Red paint and chrome bars to the custom graphics. The Quist is ready to go big, right out of the box.\nFull chromoly frame with integrated head tube and mid BB shell. 20.5\" top tube.\nFull chromoly fork with 1-piece, internally threaded steerer tube & tapered legs. 32mm offset.\nHaro full chromoly 9\" rise, 2-piece bars.\nHaro Baseline top load stem.\nHaro Baseline grips.\nHaro Baseline 170mm 3-piece chromoly cranks. 19mm spindle with sealed bearings.\nSealed front and cassette rear hub laced to 36H double wall rims.\nGyro detangler with 990-style brakes.\nHaro Baseline 2-piece seat with alloy post.\nHaro HPF tires 20x2.2\" front & rear.",
